// rafan's point from planning: everyone uses ai, everyone calls it larp, so nobody admits it or learns to use it well
---
<header>
  <div class="section">how to work</div>
  <h2>the ai thing</h2>
</header>
<div class="tab">
  <p class="big">everyone uses it. nobody admits it.</p>
  <ul>
    <li class="step">calling it larp doesn’t stop anyone using it. it just stops people talking about <em>how</em></li>
    <li class="step">so nobody learns the difference between skipping the work and doing it faster</li>
    <li class="step">here, say how you used it. it’s part of the demo</li>
  </ul>
</div>
<style>
  .tab { width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .big { font-size: 64px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 0 0 30px; }
  ul { font-size: 32px; list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  li { margin: 14px 0; padding-left: 26px; border-left: 5px solid var(--accent); }
  li em { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); }
  li:last-child { border-left-color: var(--good); color: var(--good); font-weight: 650; }
